{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-09_12-07-35-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('map.json'))\np['version']=3\np['surfaces'].append({\n \\\"entry_point\\\":\\\"processHeartbeat / net_transport heartbeat fast path\\\",\n \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\n \\\"reason\\\":\\\"Sourced discrepancy in the appendEntries entry paths: processRPC calls checkRPCHeader before dispatching AppendEntries (raft.go:1390-1413), but the heartbeat fast path processHeartbeat calls appendEntries directly with no read of checkRPCHeader (raft.go:1415-1436), and net_transport routes any pure AppendEntries heartbeat (Term \"'!= 0, leader addr present, no entries, no prev-log fields, LeaderCommitIndex 0) to that handler (net_transport.go:660-686, 724-733). An AppendEntries whose RPCHeader.ProtocolVersion is outside the supported window that checkRPCHeader rejects on the normal path would therefore still be accepted on the fast path, where appendEntries can step the receiver down, persist a newer term, set the sender as known leader and refresh lastContact. Whether the window outside the fast path'\"'s route is reachable with a legal peer and what consequence it has is not established.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S40\\\",\\\"S41\\\",\\\"S42\\\",\\\"S43\\\"],\n \\\"high_consequence\\\":True})\nopen('map.json','w').write(json.dumps(p,indent=1))\nprint('version',p['version'],'surfaces',len(p['surfaces']))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
